Z||000000||Oreif||02-25-2000||02:25 AM||||A friend who collects sales brochures brought in his 1988 "Pontiac Hot Ones" sales flyer. It describes the Fieros and mentions that mid-year for 1988 the GT's and Formulas<BR>Get an electronic pump attached to the rack for "speed sensitive power steering" Does anyone know if they ever actually made it onto a productio car? They even showed a pic of it! I wonder if the rack was able to be ordered through Pontiac. They also have an add on the same page for a 16-valve 370hp SD4 and a phone number to call to get your own parts!||||reg||3
Z||000001||Standard||02-25-2000||02:38 AM||||All 1988 Fieros have mounts for power steering.  All of the Fiero's that actually had power steering units installed were stripped of the equipment before they were sold, due to pontiac canceling the car.  <BR>It was an electro-hydraulic speed sensitive unit, also heard that one reason it wasn't used was that it was pretty noisy.  <BR>I don't think you really need power steering on the Fiero, the front end is so light.  I don't like power steering, anyways.  Makes me feel too isolated.  Can't feel the road.   ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||02-25-2000||04:55 AM||||13 were produced.  Probably all in the back of GM execs garages under cover, no miles, etc.  Supposedly there were as many as 100 p/s units sold by GM aftermarket, but who knows?||||reg||1
Z||000003||cobra427||02-26-2000||12:35 AM||||I have seen two Fieros with the power steering. One at Englishtown,NJ and one in Rutland, Ma.||||reg||1
